event: response.output_text.delta
data: {"type":"response.output_text.delta","content_index":0,"delta":".\n","item_id":"msg_083d06ea13b4890d016aa3e50ca58487d2ad72684821eba7a8","logprobs":[],"obfuscation":"vGV2V9d2lkTz6l","output_index":1,"sequence_number":6020}

event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_083d06ea13b4890d016aa3e50ca58487d2ad72684821eba7a8","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6021,"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for the program boundaries of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting). Each POST represents one\n    batch program invocation, not an individual transaction or an entire job schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, JSON serialization, and status codes are chosen transport\n    conventions, not COBOL behavior. Request arrays supply sequential input\n    files in array order. Indexed master files are environment-provided\n    persistent dependencies, not implicitly created from requests. Output\n    arrays expose records written by the program. No sorting, backup, merge,\n    load, retry, rollback, or atomic commit is included.\n\n    Character fields are transported without trimming; shorter strings are\n    right-padded with spaces to their COBOL picture width. Numeric identifiers\n    are digit strings preserving leading zeroes. Decimal numbers represent\n    valid numeric picture values, including negative amounts and rates.\n    No calendar-date, card-number, transaction-type, or category validation is\n    imposed unless described for the particular program. Empty arrays and\n    unknown keys remain representable.\n\n    Runtime-generated timestamps use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, derived from\n    CURRENT-DATE without a transported timezone. They are not RFC 3339 values.\nx-preconditions:\n  - The COBOL programs, copybooks, file runtime, and file assignments must be available.\n  - Indexed files must support the declared keys and open modes; sequential files must support their record lengths.\n  - Each invocation needs fresh program working storage equivalent to a batch execution.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    CEE3ABD is referenced but not supplied. Error branches display diagnostics\n    and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and timing 0; actual termination and runtime\n    error delivery depend on that external service.\n  - |\n    Arithmetic uses fixed pictures without ON SIZE ERROR or ROUNDED. Fractional\n    digits are discarded on assignment rather than contractually rounded to\n    nearest. Overflow, invalid physical numeric encodings, character encoding,\n    and compiler/runtime-specific file behavior are not specified here.\n  - |\n    JCL is dependency and orchestration evidence, not proof of execution.\n    TRANBKP uses REPROC and IDCAMS to back up and recreate the transaction\n    master. COMBTRAN sorts backup and system transactions by ID and loads them\n    with IDCAMS. Neither is invoked by these operations. REPROC references\n    REPROCT control input that is not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL unloads, filters processing dates, and sorts card numbers using\n    ZD, although COBOL card numbers are X(16). It contains duplicate STEP05R\n    labels. This contract does not execute that preprocessing or exclude\n    nonnumeric card values.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process the daily transaction input in sequence\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN02C boundary. DALYTRAN is sequential input; XREFFILE is\n        indexed input by card number; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed by transaction ID but is opened OUTPUT, not I-O or\n        EXTEND. DALYREJS is sequential OUTPUT. Consequently this is not a\n        promised append-to-existing-master operation; opening OUTPUT can\n        initialize or replace the output according to the file runtime.\n\n        For each daily record the validation reason is cleared. An invalid-key\n        cross-reference read gives 0100 and skips account validation. An\n        invalid-key account read gives 0101. For an account found, temporary\n        balance = currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount, held in\n        S9(9)V99. A credit limit smaller than that result gives 0102. Then\n        expirationDate is compared as characters with originalTimestamp(1:10);\n        expirationDate smaller than that prefix gives 0103, overwriting 0102\n        if both fail. Equality passes both comparisons. Account active status,\n        cash credit limit, type and category existence are not validated.\n\n        A rejected record is copied to DALYREJS with its four-digit reason and\n        76-character padded description, and processing continues. The\n        processed count includes accepted and rejected input records.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 if any rejects occurred; the\n        no-reject branch does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        For an accepted record, fields are copied to the transaction output,\n        except processingTimestamp is replaced with the current timestamp.\n        First the category balance keyed by mapped account, type and category\n        is created from initialized data if missing (status 23), or incremented\n        by amount if present. Next amount is added to account currentBalance.\n        Nonnegative amount is added to currentCycleCredit; negative amount is\n        added, still negative, to currentCycleDebit. Finally the transaction\n        is written to TRANFILE. These actions are ordered and not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, \"ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND\", but does not enter the reject-writing branch or increment\n        the reject count: the transaction write still follows. There is no\n        duplicate-ID business validation. A failed transaction write, including\n        an indexed duplicate-key failure, takes the fatal I/O path after the\n        earlier balance update attempts.\n      x-dependencies:\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: input-output\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; duplicates are permitted as input.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Program returned, possibly with per-record rejections. HTTP 200\n            represents completed batch processing, not acceptance of every\n            input record or successful account rewrites.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, rejects, processedCount, rejectedCount]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to the output indexed transaction file, exposed in write order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Explicitly 4 when rejectedCount is positive; otherwise runtime return code if available.\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. Non-00 open/close statuses, daily read\n            statuses other than 00/10, category read statuses other than 00/23,\n            category write/rewrite failures, reject write failures and\n            transaction write failures call the abend service. Validation\n            cross-reference/account reads and account rewrites do not have\n            general status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n            Earlier file effects may remain. Closing DALYREJS mistakenly\n            displays XREFFILE status, not DALYREJS status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBACT04C boundary. Reads TCATBALF sequentially in indexed\n        key order (account, type, category); reads ACCTFILE by account and\n        XREFFILE by its alternate account key at account changes. ACCTFILE is\n        opened I-O; TCATBALF, XREFFILE and DISCGRP are INPUT. TRANSACT is\n        sequential OUTPUT, separate from the posting program's indexed\n        TRANFILE. Generated transactions are not posted or merged by this\n        operation, and category balances are not modified.\n\n        For each category balance, look up the account group, type and category\n        in DISCGRP. Status 23 causes a second lookup with group \"DEFAULT\"\n        space-padded to ten characters and the same type/category. A missing\n        default is fatal. A zero rate produces no transaction. For any nonzero\n        rate compute monthlyInterest = categoryBalance * interestRate / 1200,\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED. Generate a transaction even when\n        that computed amount is zero or negative; add it to an S9(9)V99 account\n        interest accumulator. Fee computation is an empty paragraph.\n\n        Generated IDs concatenate all ten parameter characters and an\n        incrementing six-digit suffix starting at 000001. Type is \"01\",\n        numeric category is 0005, source is \"System\", description begins\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is the\n        computed interest, merchant ID is zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are\n        spaces, and card number comes from the account-key cross-reference.\n        Both timestamps are the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        At each change after the first account, add accumulated interest to\n        the previous account currentBalance, clear its currentCycleCredit and\n        currentCycleDebit, and rewrite it. Critically, the apparent EOF update\n        ELSE branch is not reached by normal loop flow: the read sets EOF\n        inside the other branch and the loop exits. The last account is not\n        rewritten. With one account, interest transactions can be generated\n        with no account update; empty input generates no transactions and\n        rewrites no account.\n      x-dependencies:\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: sequential-indexed-input\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          alternateKey: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        DISCGRP:\n          access: input\n          key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureRate'\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path but the program\n          assigns XREFFILE. Successful alternate-key reads require runtime\n          configuration; the corpus does not demonstrate that configuration.\n        - |\n          Parameter length is declared S9(4) COMP but never inspected. The\n          transport supplies ten characters and sets linkage length to ten.\n          The JCL example is 2022071800; this is an ID prefix, not a validated date.\n        - |\n          Suffix overflow after 999999 and arithmetic overflow have no handled\n          branch. Description tails and filler are not explicitly initialized\n          when constructing output records; their exact bytes are not promised.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10), padded to ten characters; arbitrary characters and blanks are permitted.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Generated sequential output is available; account effects follow account-change logic, not a final-account flush.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. All opens/closes require 00; category\n            sequential reads allow 00/10. Missing account or account-key\n            cross-reference, non-00 account rewrite, failed default disclosure\n            lookup, other disclosure read errors and failed transaction writes\n            call the abend service. Output records and previous account\n            rewrites can already exist.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction report records\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN03C boundary, not TRANREPT JCL. The request supplies\n        sequential TRANFILE records and DATEPARM records. Only the first\n        DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is\n        ignored, and positions 12-21 are end date. EOF on DATEPARM ends\n        processing without reading transactions. Dates are compared as\n        characters, not validated as calendar dates; reversed ranges are\n        representable and not rejected.\n\n        The program compares processingTimestamp(1:10) inclusively to the\n        range. An out-of-range record executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the\n        remainder of the loop's sentence. No sorting occurs. Contiguous card\n        changes, not account-ID changes, trigger an \"Account Total\" and a new\n        cross-reference lookup. Supply card-grouped input for conventional\n        grouping; ungrouped input remains representable and yields repeated\n        groups. Type and type/category descriptions are looked up for every\n        included detail. Unknown lookup keys take the fatal branch.\n\n        Output is TRANREPT opened OUTPUT, with 133-character records.\n        Detail fields are transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and\n        first 15 description characters, four-digit category and first 29\n        category-description characters, source, and amount edited as\n        -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ. Headers use DALYREPT, Daily Transaction Report,\n        the range and column labels. Total amounts use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n\n        The first detail emits four header records. Before each detail, a page\n        break occurs only when lineCounter modulo 20 is zero. Headers, totals\n        and separator lines increment the counter as coded, so twenty is not\n        a guaranteed number of details or an enforced maximum page length.\n        Page totals are added into the grand total and reset. Account totals\n        reset on card changes and do not contribute separately to grand total.\n\n        EOF is checked after the date comparison. When the EOF iteration\n        passes that comparison, the program adds TRAN-AMT again to page and\n        account totals, then writes page and grand totals, with no final\n        account total. If the read buffer retains the last included record,\n        its amount is therefore counted twice in the final totals. If the\n        retained record is outside the range, NEXT SENTENCE skips final\n        totals. Do not interpret the output as a corrected aggregation.\n        Empty input buffer behavior and EOF buffer contents are runtime\n        dependent; this contract preserves report lines rather than promising\n        normalized totals.\n      x-dependencies:\n        CARDXREF:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        TRANTYPE:\n          access: input\n          key: typeCode\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n        TRANCATG:\n          access: input\n          key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; empty means immediate EOF. Extra records are ignored.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: Right-padded to 80 characters. No separator, date-format or date-order validation.\n                    examples: ['2022-01-01 2022-07-06']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program returned; lines preserve the actual formatting and control-flow totals, including edge cases.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path: open/close failure, sequential read\n            other than 00/10, report write failure, or INVALID KEY on card,\n            type or category lookup. Lookup invalid-key diagnostics set\n            IO-STATUS to 23 before the abend call. Other lookup statuses are\n            not generally checked by these paragraphs. Partial report output\n            may already exist; no master balances are changed.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportError:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP rejection for malformed JSON or a value not representable\n        by the declared transport schema. This is not a COBOL validation\n        reason. No legacy transport-error payload exists.\n  schemas:\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(10)V99.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); overflow is not handled.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2), not constrained to a known-code enumeration.\n    CardNumber:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 16\n      description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or existing cards.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26); arbitrary text is representable, and input is not date-validated.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      description: |\n        Semantic serialization of CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y, each 350 characters in\n        the legacy record representation. All business fields are supplied.\n        Optional filler defaults to spaces on input; rejected records preserve\n        it. Posted and generated output filler bytes are not explicitly moved\n        by the source and are exposed only if available.\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: |\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n            0103 takes precedence over 0102. Internal 0109 is not a DALYREJS reason.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 76\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: Corresponding literal padded with spaces; combined with reasonCode forms the 80-character trailer.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT01Y persistent 300-character account record. Fields not changed by an operation remain as stored.\n      required:\n        - accountId\n        - activeStatus\n        - currentBalance\n        - creditLimit\n        - cashCreditLimit\n        - openDate\n        - expirationDate\n        - reissueDate\n        - currentCycleCredit\n        - currentCycleDebit\n        - addressZip\n        - groupId\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE, compared lexically during posting.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureRate:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, interestRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; signed rate used in balance * rate / 1200.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Captured DISPLAY output, when available, in emission order. Programs\n        display start/end banners, errors and file statuses; interest and\n        reporting also display input records. These are not normalized\n        business-error objects.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Chosen transport envelope for an invocation that did not return\n        normally. Only available observations are included. HTTP 500 does\n        not imply that any writes were undone or that CEE3ABD was available.\n        No universal legacy error payload or partial-output recovery facility\n        is defined by the corpus.\n      properties:\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the program's CEE3ABD call was observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 2\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: Raw two-character file status if available; not necessarily numeric.\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing program paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n"}

event: response.content_part.done
data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_083d06ea13b4890d016aa3e50ca58487d2ad72684821eba7a8","output_index":1,"part":{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for the program boundaries of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting). Each POST represents one\n    batch program invocation, not an individual transaction or an entire job schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, JSON serialization, and status codes are chosen transport\n    conventions, not COBOL behavior. Request arrays supply sequential input\n    files in array order. Indexed master files are environment-provided\n    persistent dependencies, not implicitly created from requests. Output\n    arrays expose records written by the program. No sorting, backup, merge,\n    load, retry, rollback, or atomic commit is included.\n\n    Character fields are transported without trimming; shorter strings are\n    right-padded with spaces to their COBOL picture width. Numeric identifiers\n    are digit strings preserving leading zeroes. Decimal numbers represent\n    valid numeric picture values, including negative amounts and rates.\n    No calendar-date, card-number, transaction-type, or category validation is\n    imposed unless described for the particular program. Empty arrays and\n    unknown keys remain representable.\n\n    Runtime-generated timestamps use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, derived from\n    CURRENT-DATE without a transported timezone. They are not RFC 3339 values.\nx-preconditions:\n  - The COBOL programs, copybooks, file runtime, and file assignments must be available.\n  - Indexed files must support the declared keys and open modes; sequential files must support their record lengths.\n  - Each invocation needs fresh program working storage equivalent to a batch execution.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    CEE3ABD is referenced but not supplied. Error branches display diagnostics\n    and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and timing 0; actual termination and runtime\n    error delivery depend on that external service.\n  - |\n    Arithmetic uses fixed pictures without ON SIZE ERROR or ROUNDED. Fractional\n    digits are discarded on assignment rather than contractually rounded to\n    nearest. Overflow, invalid physical numeric encodings, character encoding,\n    and compiler/runtime-specific file behavior are not specified here.\n  - |\n    JCL is dependency and orchestration evidence, not proof of execution.\n    TRANBKP uses REPROC and IDCAMS to back up and recreate the transaction\n    master. COMBTRAN sorts backup and system transactions by ID and loads them\n    with IDCAMS. Neither is invoked by these operations. REPROC references\n    REPROCT control input that is not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL unloads, filters processing dates, and sorts card numbers using\n    ZD, although COBOL card numbers are X(16). It contains duplicate STEP05R\n    labels. This contract does not execute that preprocessing or exclude\n    nonnumeric card values.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process the daily transaction input in sequence\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN02C boundary. DALYTRAN is sequential input; XREFFILE is\n        indexed input by card number; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed by transaction ID but is opened OUTPUT, not I-O or\n        EXTEND. DALYREJS is sequential OUTPUT. Consequently this is not a\n        promised append-to-existing-master operation; opening OUTPUT can\n        initialize or replace the output according to the file runtime.\n\n        For each daily record the validation reason is cleared. An invalid-key\n        cross-reference read gives 0100 and skips account validation. An\n        invalid-key account read gives 0101. For an account found, temporary\n        balance = currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount, held in\n        S9(9)V99. A credit limit smaller than that result gives 0102. Then\n        expirationDate is compared as characters with originalTimestamp(1:10);\n        expirationDate smaller than that prefix gives 0103, overwriting 0102\n        if both fail. Equality passes both comparisons. Account active status,\n        cash credit limit, type and category existence are not validated.\n\n        A rejected record is copied to DALYREJS with its four-digit reason and\n        76-character padded description, and processing continues. The\n        processed count includes accepted and rejected input records.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 if any rejects occurred; the\n        no-reject branch does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        For an accepted record, fields are copied to the transaction output,\n        except processingTimestamp is replaced with the current timestamp.\n        First the category balance keyed by mapped account, type and category\n        is created from initialized data if missing (status 23), or incremented\n        by amount if present. Next amount is added to account currentBalance.\n        Nonnegative amount is added to currentCycleCredit; negative amount is\n        added, still negative, to currentCycleDebit. Finally the transaction\n        is written to TRANFILE. These actions are ordered and not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, \"ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND\", but does not enter the reject-writing branch or increment\n        the reject count: the transaction write still follows. There is no\n        duplicate-ID business validation. A failed transaction write, including\n        an indexed duplicate-key failure, takes the fatal I/O path after the\n        earlier balance update attempts.\n      x-dependencies:\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: input-output\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; duplicates are permitted as input.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Program returned, possibly with per-record rejections. HTTP 200\n            represents completed batch processing, not acceptance of every\n            input record or successful account rewrites.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, rejects, processedCount, rejectedCount]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to the output indexed transaction file, exposed in write order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Explicitly 4 when rejectedCount is positive; otherwise runtime return code if available.\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. Non-00 open/close statuses, daily read\n            statuses other than 00/10, category read statuses other than 00/23,\n            category write/rewrite failures, reject write failures and\n            transaction write failures call the abend service. Validation\n            cross-reference/account reads and account rewrites do not have\n            general status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n            Earlier file effects may remain. Closing DALYREJS mistakenly\n            displays XREFFILE status, not DALYREJS status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBACT04C boundary. Reads TCATBALF sequentially in indexed\n        key order (account, type, category); reads ACCTFILE by account and\n        XREFFILE by its alternate account key at account changes. ACCTFILE is\n        opened I-O; TCATBALF, XREFFILE and DISCGRP are INPUT. TRANSACT is\n        sequential OUTPUT, separate from the posting program's indexed\n        TRANFILE. Generated transactions are not posted or merged by this\n        operation, and category balances are not modified.\n\n        For each category balance, look up the account group, type and category\n        in DISCGRP. Status 23 causes a second lookup with group \"DEFAULT\"\n        space-padded to ten characters and the same type/category. A missing\n        default is fatal. A zero rate produces no transaction. For any nonzero\n        rate compute monthlyInterest = categoryBalance * interestRate / 1200,\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED. Generate a transaction even when\n        that computed amount is zero or negative; add it to an S9(9)V99 account\n        interest accumulator. Fee computation is an empty paragraph.\n\n        Generated IDs concatenate all ten parameter characters and an\n        incrementing six-digit suffix starting at 000001. Type is \"01\",\n        numeric category is 0005, source is \"System\", description begins\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is the\n        computed interest, merchant ID is zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are\n        spaces, and card number comes from the account-key cross-reference.\n        Both timestamps are the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        At each change after the first account, add accumulated interest to\n        the previous account currentBalance, clear its currentCycleCredit and\n        currentCycleDebit, and rewrite it. Critically, the apparent EOF update\n        ELSE branch is not reached by normal loop flow: the read sets EOF\n        inside the other branch and the loop exits. The last account is not\n        rewritten. With one account, interest transactions can be generated\n        with no account update; empty input generates no transactions and\n        rewrites no account.\n      x-dependencies:\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: sequential-indexed-input\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          alternateKey: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        DISCGRP:\n          access: input\n          key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureRate'\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path but the program\n          assigns XREFFILE. Successful alternate-key reads require runtime\n          configuration; the corpus does not demonstrate that configuration.\n        - |\n          Parameter length is declared S9(4) COMP but never inspected. The\n          transport supplies ten characters and sets linkage length to ten.\n          The JCL example is 2022071800; this is an ID prefix, not a validated date.\n        - |\n          Suffix overflow after 999999 and arithmetic overflow have no handled\n          branch. Description tails and filler are not explicitly initialized\n          when constructing output records; their exact bytes are not promised.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10), padded to ten characters; arbitrary characters and blanks are permitted.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Generated sequential output is available; account effects follow account-change logic, not a final-account flush.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. All opens/closes require 00; category\n            sequential reads allow 00/10. Missing account or account-key\n            cross-reference, non-00 account rewrite, failed default disclosure\n            lookup, other disclosure read errors and failed transaction writes\n            call the abend service. Output records and previous account\n            rewrites can already exist.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction report records\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN03C boundary, not TRANREPT JCL. The request supplies\n        sequential TRANFILE records and DATEPARM records. Only the first\n        DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is\n        ignored, and positions 12-21 are end date. EOF on DATEPARM ends\n        processing without reading transactions. Dates are compared as\n        characters, not validated as calendar dates; reversed ranges are\n        representable and not rejected.\n\n        The program compares processingTimestamp(1:10) inclusively to the\n        range. An out-of-range record executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the\n        remainder of the loop's sentence. No sorting occurs. Contiguous card\n        changes, not account-ID changes, trigger an \"Account Total\" and a new\n        cross-reference lookup. Supply card-grouped input for conventional\n        grouping; ungrouped input remains representable and yields repeated\n        groups. Type and type/category descriptions are looked up for every\n        included detail. Unknown lookup keys take the fatal branch.\n\n        Output is TRANREPT opened OUTPUT, with 133-character records.\n        Detail fields are transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and\n        first 15 description characters, four-digit category and first 29\n        category-description characters, source, and amount edited as\n        -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ. Headers use DALYREPT, Daily Transaction Report,\n        the range and column labels. Total amounts use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n\n        The first detail emits four header records. Before each detail, a page\n        break occurs only when lineCounter modulo 20 is zero. Headers, totals\n        and separator lines increment the counter as coded, so twenty is not\n        a guaranteed number of details or an enforced maximum page length.\n        Page totals are added into the grand total and reset. Account totals\n        reset on card changes and do not contribute separately to grand total.\n\n        EOF is checked after the date comparison. When the EOF iteration\n        passes that comparison, the program adds TRAN-AMT again to page and\n        account totals, then writes page and grand totals, with no final\n        account total. If the read buffer retains the last included record,\n        its amount is therefore counted twice in the final totals. If the\n        retained record is outside the range, NEXT SENTENCE skips final\n        totals. Do not interpret the output as a corrected aggregation.\n        Empty input buffer behavior and EOF buffer contents are runtime\n        dependent; this contract preserves report lines rather than promising\n        normalized totals.\n      x-dependencies:\n        CARDXREF:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        TRANTYPE:\n          access: input\n          key: typeCode\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n        TRANCATG:\n          access: input\n          key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; empty means immediate EOF. Extra records are ignored.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: Right-padded to 80 characters. No separator, date-format or date-order validation.\n                    examples: ['2022-01-01 2022-07-06']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program returned; lines preserve the actual formatting and control-flow totals, including edge cases.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path: open/close failure, sequential read\n            other than 00/10, report write failure, or INVALID KEY on card,\n            type or category lookup. Lookup invalid-key diagnostics set\n            IO-STATUS to 23 before the abend call. Other lookup statuses are\n            not generally checked by these paragraphs. Partial report output\n            may already exist; no master balances are changed.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportError:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP rejection for malformed JSON or a value not representable\n        by the declared transport schema. This is not a COBOL validation\n        reason. No legacy transport-error payload exists.\n  schemas:\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(10)V99.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); overflow is not handled.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2), not constrained to a known-code enumeration.\n    CardNumber:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 16\n      description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or existing cards.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26); arbitrary text is representable, and input is not date-validated.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      description: |\n        Semantic serialization of CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y, each 350 characters in\n        the legacy record representation. All business fields are supplied.\n        Optional filler defaults to spaces on input; rejected records preserve\n        it. Posted and generated output filler bytes are not explicitly moved\n        by the source and are exposed only if available.\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: |\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n            0103 takes precedence over 0102. Internal 0109 is not a DALYREJS reason.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 76\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: Corresponding literal padded with spaces; combined with reasonCode forms the 80-character trailer.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT01Y persistent 300-character account record. Fields not changed by an operation remain as stored.\n      required:\n        - accountId\n        - activeStatus\n        - currentBalance\n        - creditLimit\n        - cashCreditLimit\n        - openDate\n        - expirationDate\n        - reissueDate\n        - currentCycleCredit\n        - currentCycleDebit\n        - addressZip\n        - groupId\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE, compared lexically during posting.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureRate:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, interestRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; signed rate used in balance * rate / 1200.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Captured DISPLAY output, when available, in emission order. Programs\n        display start/end banners, errors and file statuses; interest and\n        reporting also display input records. These are not normalized\n        business-error objects.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Chosen transport envelope for an invocation that did not return\n        normally. Only available observations are included. HTTP 500 does\n        not imply that any writes were undone or that CEE3ABD was available.\n        No universal legacy error payload or partial-output recovery facility\n        is defined by the corpus.\n      properties:\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the program's CEE3ABD call was observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 2\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: Raw two-character file status if available; not necessarily numeric.\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing program paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n"},"sequence_number":6022}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"msg_083d06ea13b4890d016aa3e50ca58487d2ad72684821eba7a8","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Batch Transaction API\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for the program boundaries of CBTRN02C (posting), CBACT04C\n    (interest generation), and CBTRN03C (reporting). Each POST represents one\n    batch program invocation, not an individual transaction or an entire job schedule.\n\n    HTTP paths, JSON serialization, and status codes are chosen transport\n    conventions, not COBOL behavior. Request arrays supply sequential input\n    files in array order. Indexed master files are environment-provided\n    persistent dependencies, not implicitly created from requests. Output\n    arrays expose records written by the program. No sorting, backup, merge,\n    load, retry, rollback, or atomic commit is included.\n\n    Character fields are transported without trimming; shorter strings are\n    right-padded with spaces to their COBOL picture width. Numeric identifiers\n    are digit strings preserving leading zeroes. Decimal numbers represent\n    valid numeric picture values, including negative amounts and rates.\n    No calendar-date, card-number, transaction-type, or category validation is\n    imposed unless described for the particular program. Empty arrays and\n    unknown keys remain representable.\n\n    Runtime-generated timestamps use YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000, derived from\n    CURRENT-DATE without a transported timezone. They are not RFC 3339 values.\nx-preconditions:\n  - The COBOL programs, copybooks, file runtime, and file assignments must be available.\n  - Indexed files must support the declared keys and open modes; sequential files must support their record lengths.\n  - Each invocation needs fresh program working storage equivalent to a batch execution.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    CEE3ABD is referenced but not supplied. Error branches display diagnostics\n    and call CEE3ABD with code 999 and timing 0; actual termination and runtime\n    error delivery depend on that external service.\n  - |\n    Arithmetic uses fixed pictures without ON SIZE ERROR or ROUNDED. Fractional\n    digits are discarded on assignment rather than contractually rounded to\n    nearest. Overflow, invalid physical numeric encodings, character encoding,\n    and compiler/runtime-specific file behavior are not specified here.\n  - |\n    JCL is dependency and orchestration evidence, not proof of execution.\n    TRANBKP uses REPROC and IDCAMS to back up and recreate the transaction\n    master. COMBTRAN sorts backup and system transactions by ID and loads them\n    with IDCAMS. Neither is invoked by these operations. REPROC references\n    REPROCT control input that is not supplied.\n  - |\n    TRANREPT JCL unloads, filters processing dates, and sorts card numbers using\n    ZD, although COBOL card numbers are X(16). It contains duplicate STEP05R\n    labels. This contract does not execute that preprocessing or exclude\n    nonnumeric card values.\npaths:\n  /transaction-postings:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Process the daily transaction input in sequence\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN02C boundary. DALYTRAN is sequential input; XREFFILE is\n        indexed input by card number; ACCTFILE and TCATBALF are opened I-O.\n        TRANFILE is indexed by transaction ID but is opened OUTPUT, not I-O or\n        EXTEND. DALYREJS is sequential OUTPUT. Consequently this is not a\n        promised append-to-existing-master operation; opening OUTPUT can\n        initialize or replace the output according to the file runtime.\n\n        For each daily record the validation reason is cleared. An invalid-key\n        cross-reference read gives 0100 and skips account validation. An\n        invalid-key account read gives 0101. For an account found, temporary\n        balance = currentCycleCredit - currentCycleDebit + amount, held in\n        S9(9)V99. A credit limit smaller than that result gives 0102. Then\n        expirationDate is compared as characters with originalTimestamp(1:10);\n        expirationDate smaller than that prefix gives 0103, overwriting 0102\n        if both fail. Equality passes both comparisons. Account active status,\n        cash credit limit, type and category existence are not validated.\n\n        A rejected record is copied to DALYREJS with its four-digit reason and\n        76-character padded description, and processing continues. The\n        processed count includes accepted and rejected input records.\n        RETURN-CODE is explicitly set to 4 if any rejects occurred; the\n        no-reject branch does not explicitly assign RETURN-CODE.\n\n        For an accepted record, fields are copied to the transaction output,\n        except processingTimestamp is replaced with the current timestamp.\n        First the category balance keyed by mapped account, type and category\n        is created from initialized data if missing (status 23), or incremented\n        by amount if present. Next amount is added to account currentBalance.\n        Nonnegative amount is added to currentCycleCredit; negative amount is\n        added, still negative, to currentCycleDebit. Finally the transaction\n        is written to TRANFILE. These actions are ordered and not atomic.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, \"ACCOUNT RECORD\n        NOT FOUND\", but does not enter the reject-writing branch or increment\n        the reject count: the transaction write still follows. There is no\n        duplicate-ID business validation. A failed transaction write, including\n        an indexed duplicate-key failure, takes the fatal I/O path after the\n        earlier balance update attempts.\n      x-dependencies:\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: input-output\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  description: DALYTRAN records in read order; duplicates are permitted as input.\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: |\n            Program returned, possibly with per-record rejections. HTTP 200\n            represents completed batch processing, not acceptance of every\n            input record or successful account rewrites.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions, rejects, processedCount, rejectedCount]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    description: Records successfully written to the output indexed transaction file, exposed in write order.\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  rejects:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/RejectedTransaction'\n                  processedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  rejectedCount:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Counter'\n                  returnCode:\n                    type: integer\n                    description: Explicitly 4 when rejectedCount is positive; otherwise runtime return code if available.\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. Non-00 open/close statuses, daily read\n            statuses other than 00/10, category read statuses other than 00/23,\n            category write/rewrite failures, reject write failures and\n            transaction write failures call the abend service. Validation\n            cross-reference/account reads and account rewrites do not have\n            general status checks beyond their INVALID KEY clauses.\n            Earlier file effects may remain. Closing DALYREJS mistakenly\n            displays XREFFILE status, not DALYREJS status.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-transaction-generations:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Generate system interest transactions from category balances\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBACT04C boundary. Reads TCATBALF sequentially in indexed\n        key order (account, type, category); reads ACCTFILE by account and\n        XREFFILE by its alternate account key at account changes. ACCTFILE is\n        opened I-O; TCATBALF, XREFFILE and DISCGRP are INPUT. TRANSACT is\n        sequential OUTPUT, separate from the posting program's indexed\n        TRANFILE. Generated transactions are not posted or merged by this\n        operation, and category balances are not modified.\n\n        For each category balance, look up the account group, type and category\n        in DISCGRP. Status 23 causes a second lookup with group \"DEFAULT\"\n        space-padded to ten characters and the same type/category. A missing\n        default is fatal. A zero rate produces no transaction. For any nonzero\n        rate compute monthlyInterest = categoryBalance * interestRate / 1200,\n        assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED. Generate a transaction even when\n        that computed amount is zero or negative; add it to an S9(9)V99 account\n        interest accumulator. Fee computation is an empty paragraph.\n\n        Generated IDs concatenate all ten parameter characters and an\n        incrementing six-digit suffix starting at 000001. Type is \"01\",\n        numeric category is 0005, source is \"System\", description begins\n        \"Int. for a/c \" followed by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is the\n        computed interest, merchant ID is zero, merchant name/city/ZIP are\n        spaces, and card number comes from the account-key cross-reference.\n        Both timestamps are the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        At each change after the first account, add accumulated interest to\n        the previous account currentBalance, clear its currentCycleCredit and\n        currentCycleDebit, and rewrite it. Critically, the apparent EOF update\n        ELSE branch is not reached by normal loop flow: the read sets EOF\n        inside the other branch and the loop exits. The last account is not\n        rewritten. With one account, interest transactions can be generated\n        with no account update; empty input generates no transactions and\n        rewrites no account.\n      x-dependencies:\n        TCATBALF:\n          access: sequential-indexed-input\n          key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n        ACCTFILE:\n          access: input-output\n          key: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n        XREFFILE:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          alternateKey: accountId\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        DISCGRP:\n          access: input\n          key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureRate'\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC supplies XREFFIL1 as an alternate-index path but the program\n          assigns XREFFILE. Successful alternate-key reads require runtime\n          configuration; the corpus does not demonstrate that configuration.\n        - |\n          Parameter length is declared S9(4) COMP but never inspected. The\n          transport supplies ten characters and sets linkage length to ten.\n          The JCL example is 2022071800; this is an ID prefix, not a validated date.\n        - |\n          Suffix overflow after 999999 and arithmetic overflow have no handled\n          branch. Description tails and filler are not explicitly initialized\n          when constructing output records; their exact bytes are not promised.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactionIdPrefix]\n              properties:\n                transactionIdPrefix:\n                  type: string\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: PARM-DATE PIC X(10), padded to ten characters; arbitrary characters and blanks are permitted.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Generated sequential output is available; account effects follow account-change logic, not a final-account flush.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [transactions]\n                properties:\n                  transactions:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path. All opens/closes require 00; category\n            sequential reads allow 00/10. Missing account or account-key\n            cross-reference, non-00 account rewrite, failed default disclosure\n            lookup, other disclosure read errors and failed transaction writes\n            call the abend service. Output records and previous account\n            rewrites can already exist.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-reports:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce fixed-width transaction report records\n      description: |\n        Executes the CBTRN03C boundary, not TRANREPT JCL. The request supplies\n        sequential TRANFILE records and DATEPARM records. Only the first\n        DATEPARM record is read: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is\n        ignored, and positions 12-21 are end date. EOF on DATEPARM ends\n        processing without reading transactions. Dates are compared as\n        characters, not validated as calendar dates; reversed ranges are\n        representable and not rejected.\n\n        The program compares processingTimestamp(1:10) inclusively to the\n        range. An out-of-range record executes NEXT SENTENCE, skipping the\n        remainder of the loop's sentence. No sorting occurs. Contiguous card\n        changes, not account-ID changes, trigger an \"Account Total\" and a new\n        cross-reference lookup. Supply card-grouped input for conventional\n        grouping; ungrouped input remains representable and yields repeated\n        groups. Type and type/category descriptions are looked up for every\n        included detail. Unknown lookup keys take the fatal branch.\n\n        Output is TRANREPT opened OUTPUT, with 133-character records.\n        Detail fields are transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and\n        first 15 description characters, four-digit category and first 29\n        category-description characters, source, and amount edited as\n        -ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ. Headers use DALYREPT, Daily Transaction Report,\n        the range and column labels. Total amounts use +ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ.ZZ.\n\n        The first detail emits four header records. Before each detail, a page\n        break occurs only when lineCounter modulo 20 is zero. Headers, totals\n        and separator lines increment the counter as coded, so twenty is not\n        a guaranteed number of details or an enforced maximum page length.\n        Page totals are added into the grand total and reset. Account totals\n        reset on card changes and do not contribute separately to grand total.\n\n        EOF is checked after the date comparison. When the EOF iteration\n        passes that comparison, the program adds TRAN-AMT again to page and\n        account totals, then writes page and grand totals, with no final\n        account total. If the read buffer retains the last included record,\n        its amount is therefore counted twice in the final totals. If the\n        retained record is outside the range, NEXT SENTENCE skips final\n        totals. Do not interpret the output as a corrected aggregation.\n        Empty input buffer behavior and EOF buffer contents are runtime\n        dependent; this contract preserves report lines rather than promising\n        normalized totals.\n      x-dependencies:\n        CARDXREF:\n          access: input\n          key: cardNumber\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardCrossReference'\n        TRANTYPE:\n          access: input\n          key: typeCode\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n        TRANCATG:\n          access: input\n          key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n          recordSchema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential 80-character DATEPARM records; empty means immediate EOF. Extra records are ignored.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    maxLength: 80\n                    description: Right-padded to 80 characters. No separator, date-format or date-order validation.\n                    examples: ['2022-01-01 2022-07-06']\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Report program returned; lines preserve the actual formatting and control-flow totals, including edge cases.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                type: object\n                required: [lines]\n                properties:\n                  lines:\n                    type: array\n                    items:\n                      type: string\n                      minLength: 133\n                      maxLength: 133\n                  diagnostics:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        '400':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/TransportError'\n        '500':\n          description: |\n            Fatal execution or I/O path: open/close failure, sequential read\n            other than 00/10, report write failure, or INVALID KEY on card,\n            type or category lookup. Lookup invalid-key diagnostics set\n            IO-STATUS to 23 before the abend call. Other lookup statuses are\n            not generally checked by these paragraphs. Partial report output\n            may already exist; no master balances are changed.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    TransportError:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP rejection for malformed JSON or a value not representable\n        by the declared transport schema. This is not a COBOL validation\n        reason. No legacy transport-error payload exists.\n  schemas:\n    Amount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -999999999.99\n      maximum: 999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(9)V99.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: number\n      minimum: -9999999999.99\n      maximum: 9999999999.99\n      multipleOf: 0.01\n      description: PIC S9(10)V99.\n    Counter:\n      type: integer\n      minimum: 0\n      maximum: 999999999\n      description: PIC 9(9); overflow is not handled.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2), not constrained to a known-code enumeration.\n    CardNumber:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 16\n      description: PIC X(16), not restricted to digits or existing cards.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: PIC X(26); arbitrary text is representable, and input is not date-validated.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      description: |\n        Semantic serialization of CVTRA05Y or CVTRA06Y, each 350 characters in\n        the legacy record representation. All business fields are supplied.\n        Optional filler defaults to spaces on input; rejected records preserve\n        it. Posted and generated output filler bytes are not explicitly moved\n        by the source and are exposed only if available.\n      required:\n        - transactionId\n        - typeCode\n        - categoryCode\n        - source\n        - description\n        - amount\n        - merchantId\n        - merchantName\n        - merchantCity\n        - merchantZip\n        - cardNumber\n        - originalTimestamp\n        - processingTimestamp\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n    RejectedTransaction:\n      type: object\n      required: [transaction, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        transaction:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n          description: |\n            0100 INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND;\n            0101 ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND;\n            0102 OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION;\n            0103 TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION.\n            0103 takes precedence over 0102. Internal 0109 is not a DALYREJS reason.\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 76\n          maxLength: 76\n          description: Corresponding literal padded with spaces; combined with reasonCode forms the 80-character trailer.\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT01Y persistent 300-character account record. Fields not changed by an operation remain as stored.\n      required:\n        - accountId\n        - activeStatus\n        - currentBalance\n        - creditLimit\n        - cashCreditLimit\n        - openDate\n        - expirationDate\n        - reissueDate\n        - currentCycleCredit\n        - currentCycleDebit\n        - addressZip\n        - groupId\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE, compared lexically during posting.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        currentCycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        currentCycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CardCrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CardNumber'\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureRate:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50-character indexed record.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, interestRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        interestRate:\n          type: number\n          minimum: -9999.99\n          maximum: 9999.99\n          multipleOf: 0.01\n          description: PIC S9(4)V99; signed rate used in balance * rate / 1200.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60-character indexed record.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: |\n        Captured DISPLAY output, when available, in emission order. Programs\n        display start/end banners, errors and file statuses; interest and\n        reporting also display input records. These are not normalized\n        business-error objects.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Chosen transport envelope for an invocation that did not return\n        normally. Only available observations are included. HTTP 500 does\n        not imply that any writes were undone or that CEE3ABD was available.\n        No universal legacy error payload or partial-output recovery facility\n        is defined by the corpus.\n      properties:\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present when the program's CEE3ABD call was observed.\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          minLength: 2\n          maxLength: 2\n          description: Raw two-character file status if available; not necessarily numeric.\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed failing program paragraph or I/O action, if available.\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6023}

